<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lazare Hoche</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1768">1768</a>–<a href="/years/1797">1797</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lazare Hoche was a French Revolutionary general who rose from the ranks to command an army at the age of 25. He defeated the Austrians and Prussians in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> in 1793, crushed the émigré landing at Quiberon in 1795, pacified the Vendée and led the failed expedition to Ireland in 1796. As commander of the Army of Sambre-et-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> he encouraged a Cisrhenian Republic before dying of illness in September 1797.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lazare-hoche.jpg" alt="Lazare Hoche" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Louis Laneuville · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lazare_Hoche,_1801.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
